WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.210
Install ChaosEngine in one command.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.130
Everything you are about
to see is a real install,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.650
recorded on a clean Linux account.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:15.617
ChaosEngine is a portable working
contract for software agents.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.650
It gives Codex, Claude Code, Grok,
Gemini and GitHub Copilot the same skills,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.411
the same hooks and the same health checks.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.890
One command runs six steps.

00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:33.223
It resolves the latest source and
downloads only the ChaosEngine folder.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.970
It installs the core, then provisions the
tools it needs inside your home folder.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:44.537
Finally, it verifies the result with
doctor and activates your agent clients.

00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:49.403
By default, you get the lean
core and nothing else.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.930
Three add-ons are optional,
and never installed unless you ask.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:58.170
Design skills, for web,
image, motion and video work.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.110
SHAFT engine users,
for projects that test with SHAFT.

00:01:02.433 --> 00:01:06.143
And SHAFT core developers,
for contributors to SHAFT itself.

00:01:06.653 --> 00:01:08.823
It brings the users add-on with it.

00:01:10.533 --> 00:01:12.383
Each add-on has its own flag.

00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:17.383
Each add-on has a with flag to add it,
and a without flag to remove it.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.970
Or list them in the CHAOS_ENGINE_ADDONS
environment variable.

00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:25.377
Now let's do it for real.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.210
This is a fresh Linux account with an
empty project: one commit and a README.

00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:37.863
Set the installer URL,
then pipe it to bash.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.697
The core lands in seconds.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.190
Provisioning takes longer.
It fetches uv, Python,

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:58.570
Node and Java into your home folder,
so nothing touches the system.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:05.403
Installation successful.
The installer ran doctor itself:

00:02:06.313 --> 00:02:08.524
fifteen of fifteen components are healthy.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.730
It also prints a first-session brief, and
the agent hosts it found on this machine.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.857
You can run doctor yourself at any time.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:25.570
It flags graphify as degraded
and prints the repair command.

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:30.183
Now add two add-ons: design
skills and SHAFT engine users.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:33.037
Same one-liner, two extra flags.

00:02:39.733 --> 00:02:44.123
This run re-checks and re-provisions
the tools, so it takes a few minutes.

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:45.543
We've sped it up.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.170
The addons command lists what is
installed, with the flag for each one.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.890
The files live under .chaos-engine/addons.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.808
Here are the design cards.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.930
Changed your mind? The without
flag removes an add-on.

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:17.018
Removing it takes seconds.
Only design skills is left,

00:03:17.087 --> 00:03:19.617
and later upgrades keep what you selected.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.590
On Windows, use PowerShell.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.051
To pass switches, use
the script block form.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:30.370
Or set the environment variable
and keep the classic one-liner.

00:03:32.733 --> 00:03:35.183
One command. A lean, healthy core.

00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:37.423
Add-ons only when you want them.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.397
The full guide is in the SHAFT user guide.

00:03:40.927 --> 00:03:43.337
This narration uses a synthetic voice.
